WEBVTT

00:00:00.683 --> 00:00:01.875
Here's the big idea.

00:00:02.163 --> 00:00:06.640
About ninety percent of your device is
already done: the processor, the

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.331
screen, the battery, the wireless, the
software.

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:13.402
You only build the ten percent that's
left.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.519
Your connector, and your circuit.

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:18.503
The finished part is FREE-WILi 2.

00:00:18.791 --> 00:00:21.029
The part you add is called an Orca.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.125
An Orca can be anything.

00:00:24.401 --> 00:00:28.998
A network interface, a radio, or something
nobody has built yet.

00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:34.851
Snap one on, and FREE-WILi 2, a handheld
with a touchscreen, wireless,

00:00:34.851 --> 00:00:37.751
and scripting built in, becomes the tool
for the job.

00:00:39.368 --> 00:00:44.036
Every Orca plugs into the same expansion
connector, and mounts rigidly, so

00:00:44.036 --> 00:00:46.631
the connection survives a trip outside the
lab.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:52.310
A small memory on each Orca lets FREE-WILi
2 detect what's plugged in and

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:53.565
configure itself.

00:00:55.179 --> 00:00:56.205
Here is one example.

00:00:56.506 --> 00:01:02.123
SAN DIEGO Orca puts RS485, CAN and CAN FD,

00:01:02.296 --> 00:01:06.039
and both kinds of single-pair Ethernet on
one rugged connector.

00:01:06.461 --> 00:01:08.622
Wire up the harness and you're on the
network.

00:01:08.923 --> 00:01:11.288
Sniff it, script it, simulate it.

00:01:12.863 --> 00:01:17.875
Now the logging, the live display, and the
test sequence all run on the

00:01:17.875 --> 00:01:19.003
device in your hand.

00:01:19.428 --> 00:01:22.788
On its own, or plugged into your computer
over USB.

00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:25.149
Building your own?

00:01:25.449 --> 00:01:30.041
The open template repository gives you a
head start: a KiCad starter, the

00:01:30.041 --> 00:01:32.444
connector pinouts, and worked examples.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.799
Build it by hand, or hand it to an AI
agent.

00:01:37.405 --> 00:01:38.252
One handheld.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:41.275
A different tool every time you swap the
Orca.

00:01:41.692 --> 00:01:44.644
Explore the Orcas at freewili.com.

